{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Audio Classification \u2014 From k-NN on MFCCs to AST and BEATs Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: featurize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def featurize_mfcc(signal, sr, n_mfcc=13, n_mels=40, frame_len=400, hop=160):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mag = stft_magnitude(signal, frame_len, hop)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    fb = mel_filterbank(n_mels, frame_len, sr)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mels = apply_filterbank(mag, fb)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    log = log_transform(mels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [dct_ii(frame, n_mfcc) for frame in log]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: fixed-length summary"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def summarize(mfcc_frames):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = len(mfcc_frames[0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mean = [sum(f[i] for f in mfcc_frames) / len(mfcc_frames) for i in range(n)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    var = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        sum((f[i] - mean[i]) ** 2 for f in mfcc_frames) / len(mfcc_frames) for i in range(n)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return mean + var"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Simple but strong: mean + variance across time gives a 26-dim fixed embedding for a 13-coef MFCC. Runs instantly. Beat state-of-the-art NN baselines on ESC-50 as recently as 2017."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: k-NN"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def cosine(a, b):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    dot = sum(x * y for x, y in zip(a, b))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    na = math.sqrt(sum(x * x for x in a)) or 1e-12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    nb = math.sqrt(sum(x * x for x in b)) or 1e-12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return dot / (na * nb)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def knn_classify(q, bank, labels, k=5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sims = sorted(range(len(bank)), key=lambda i: -cosine(q, bank[i]))[:k]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    votes = Counter(labels[i] for i in sims)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return votes.most_common(1)[0][0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: upgrade to CNN on log-mels"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "In PyTorch:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class AudioCNN(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, n_mels=80, n_classes=50):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.body = nn.Sequential("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv2d(1, 32, 3, padding=1), nn.ReLU(), nn.MaxPool2d(2),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv2d(32, 64, 3, padding=1), nn.ReLU(), nn.MaxPool2d(2),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.Conv2d(64, 128, 3, padding=1), nn.ReLU(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            nn.AdaptiveAvgPool2d(1),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.head = nn.Linear(128, n_classes)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, x):  # x: (B, 1, T, n_mels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.head(self.body(x).flatten(1))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "3M parameters. Trains in ~10 min on ESC-50 with a single RTX 4090. 80%+ accuracy."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: the 2026 default \u2014 fine-tune BEATs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from transformers import ASTFeatureExtractor, ASTForAudioClassification"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "ext = ASTFeatureExtractor.from_pretrained(\"MIT/ast-finetuned-audioset-10-10-0.4593\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = ASTForAudioClassification.from_pretrained("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"MIT/ast-finetuned-audioset-10-10-0.4593\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    num_labels=50,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ignore_mismatched_sizes=True,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "inputs = ext(audio, sampling_rate=16000, return_tensors=\"pt\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "logits = model(**inputs).logits"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For BEATs, use `microsoft/BEATs-base` via the `beats` library; the transformers API is the same shape."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `code/main.py`. It trains the k-NN MFCC baseline on a 4-class synthetic dataset (pure tones at different pitches). Report confusion matrix.\n2. **Medium.** Replace `summarize` with [mean, var, skew, kurtosis]. Does 4-moment pooling beat mean+var on the same synthetic dataset?\n3. **Hard.** Using `torchaudio`, train a 2D CNN on ESC-50 fold 1. Report 5-fold cross-validation accuracy. Add SpecAugment (time mask = 20, freq mask = 10) and report the delta."
      ]
    }
